body:
@fogti wrote in https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/15271#issuecomment-27839902:

> If possible, I think most of the `ExecuteTemplate` invocations should be refactored, they look extremely repetitive.

I'm not sure what you would propose -- the `repo/commit_link` template *is* an earlier refactoring to eliminate the reimplementation of the links, but what's left is the data that is required to prepare the links correctly.  The statuses aren't currently populated; they don't have a lot of value in the commit set compare, but I intend to provide them later.  Do you have a suggestion?
